  "question": {
    "text": "A steady current flow in a long wire. It is bent into a circular loop of one turn and the magnetic field at the centre of the coil is<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>B</mi></math>. If the same wire is bent into a circular loop of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> turns, the magnetic field at the centre of the coil is",
